# SRG-APP-000219-WSR-000191  -  CAT II
# The web server must restrict a consistent inbound source IP for the entire
# user session.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000219-WSR-000191
group:           V-264361
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-001184
control_rev5:    SC-23

contribution:    Splunk Web has no setting that pins a user session to the source IP
                 address it began from. The product's reachable share is the source address
                 list on the Splunk Web listener, which restricts the addresses from which
                 user sessions may be established at all.

governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           web.conf [settings] acceptFrom not_matches (^|[,[:space:]])\*([,[:space:]]|$)
check:           web.conf [settings] acceptFrom not_equals *
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          web.conf [settings] acceptFrom https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Holding a user session to a consistent inbound source IP for its duration
                 - Splunk Web exposes no per-session source address binding; this is
                 carried by a reverse proxy or load balancer terminating the user session
external:        The permitted user source networks themselves - organization-defined
                 network allowlist
external:        Client address rewriting by an intermediate proxy, which determines what
                 source address Splunk Web observes - network component configuration

citation:        web.conf.spec:1080-1096 (acceptFrom = <network_acl>, "Lists a set of
                 networks or addresses from which to accept connections", rule form 4 is
                 "*", which matches anything; default "*" accept from anywhere);
                 web.conf.spec:924-930 (tools.sessions.timeout); web.conf.spec:797-804
                 (trustedIP, applicable only to SSO)
finding:         Splunk Web accepts connections from any source address, so the application
                 does not restrict the inbound source of a user session to the extent the
                 product allows.
